---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Does DMARC automatically apply to all subdomains?", "Yes, unless an sp= tag overrides the policy or the subdomain has its own DMARC record at _dmarc.subdomain.domain.com."], ["Can I set p=none for a subdomain while the root is p=reject?", "Yes, by using sp=none in the root DMARC record, or by publishing a separate DMARC record at _dmarc.subdomain.domain.com with p=none."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "DMARC Subdomain Policy",
  description: "DMARC subdomain policy (sp=): how subdomains inherit or override the root DMARC policy. RFC 7489.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "DMARC Subdomain Policy" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DMARC Subdomain Policy (sp=): How Subdomains Inherit or Override DMARC"
  description="DMARC subdomain policy (sp=): how subdomains inherit or override the root DMARC policy. RFC 7489."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DMARC Subdomain Policy</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DMARC Subdomain Policy</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">DMARC subdomain policy (sp=): how subdomains inherit or override the root DMARC policy. RFC 7489.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Scenario</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Policy applied to subdomain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>No sp= tag, root p=none</td><td>Subdomain inherits p=none</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>No sp= tag, root p=reject</td><td>Subdomain inherits p=reject</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>sp=quarantine, root p=reject</td><td>Subdomain uses p=quarantine, root uses p=reject</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DMARC record at _dmarc.sub.domain.com</td><td>Subdomain uses its own record (overrides inheritance)</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>The DMARC subdomain policy tag (sp=) defines a separate policy for subdomains of the primary domain, overriding the p= policy inherited from the root DMARC record.</p><p class='mt-3'>Without an sp= tag, all subdomains inherit the p= policy from the root domain's DMARC record, which means setting p=reject at the root also rejects failing mail from every subdomain.</p><p class='mt-3'>A subdomain can have its own DMARC record published at _dmarc.subdomain.domain.com, which overrides the inherited policy from the root domain for that specific subdomain.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The sp= tag is essential when you have subdomains that send email with their own infrastructure. Without it, tightening p=reject at the root also enforces DMARC on every subdomain, potentially breaking legitimate email from development or staging environments.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does DMARC automatically apply to all subdomains?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, unless an sp= tag overrides the policy or the subdomain has its own DMARC record at _dmarc.subdomain.domain.com.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I set p=none for a subdomain while the root is p=reject?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, by using sp=none in the root DMARC record, or by publishing a separate DMARC record at _dmarc.subdomain.domain.com with p=none.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
